The Mercedes-Benz R-Class SE trim was available in the earlier model years, particularly before the 2011 facelift. It was offered with various engine options, including the R320 CDI diesel and R500 gasoline engine. The SE trim generally represented a well-equipped, but not top-tier, version of the R-Class. Given the information available, I will base the evaluation on a representative R-Class SE from the 2006-2010 period, using data points from the R320 CDI SE and R500 SE where specified, and general R-Class data for other metrics.

